<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    DnnMigration.IntegrationTests
    ============================================================================
    SDK-style xUnit INTEGRATION-test project for the DNN 4.x -> .NET 8
    Clean/Onion Architecture backend. Unlike DnnMigration.UnitTests (which mocks
    every collaborator with Moq), this project boots the REAL DnnMigration.Api
    HTTP surface in-process through Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing's
    WebApplicationFactory<Program> and drives the live middleware/DI pipeline end
    to end over HTTP. Persistence is redirected to an EF Core InMemory store
    (Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.InMemory) so the suite never contacts a real
    SQL Server while still flowing through the genuine DnnDbContext, repositories,
    AutoMapper profiles, FluentValidation validators, JWT/BCrypt identity
    concretes and the RFC 7807 exception middleware. It exercises Portal/Module/
    User (and sibling) REST CRUD for Gate 5 (`dotnet test` run with the
    Category=Integration trait filter -> POST 201, GET 200, PUT 200, DELETE 204). The legacy
    DNN 4.9.0.85 codebase shipped zero automated tests, so this is CREATE / from
    scratch.

    Shared build configuration is centralized in backend/Directory.Build.props,
    which MSBuild imports automatically by walking up the directory tree. That
    props file is the single source of truth for TargetFramework (net8.0),
    LangVersion (12.0), Nullable, ImplicitUsings, TreatWarningsAsErrors,
    WarningsNotAsErrors (CS8618), Deterministic and GenerateDocumentationFile, so
    none of those settings are repeated here. RootNamespace/AssemblyName default
    from the file name 'DnnMigration.IntegrationTests' (matching the test
    namespaces DnnMigration.IntegrationTests.*), and IsTestProject is implied by
    Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk, so none of those are set explicitly. The only
    test-specific property declared is IsPackable=false (a test project is never
    packed/published as a package).

    Package references are limited to the integration-test toolchain:
      * Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing 8.0.11 - supplies
        WebApplicationFactory<TEntryPoint>, the in-process test host that spins up
        the real ASP.NET Core 8 pipeline; tracks the solution-wide 8.0.11 line.
      * Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.InMemory 8.0.11 - the database substitute
        registered in place of the SQL Server provider so tests are hermetic;
        matches the EF Core 8.0.11 pin used across Infrastructure.
      * Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk 17.11.1 - the VSTest platform host; without it
        `dotnet test` discovers and runs nothing on .NET 8.
      * xunit 2.9.2 - the test framework (transitively includes xunit.analyzers,
        so it is not listed separately).
      * xunit.runner.visualstudio 2.8.2 - the VS / `dotnet test` runner adapter;
        marked PrivateAssets=all (with the standard IncludeAssets set) so it is a
        test-time-only dependency and never leaks downstream.
      * FluentAssertions 6.12.2 - the fluent assertion API, pinned on the 6.x MIT
        line (NOT bumped to 7.x, which changed licensing).
    Moq is intentionally OMITTED: integration tests assert against the real
    middleware/DI graph, so no seam is faked. AutoMapper, FluentValidation, EF
    Core, BCrypt and the IdentityModel packages all flow transitively through the
    single Api ProjectReference below; restating any of them risks NU1605/version
    conflicts that would break the zero-warning Release build (Gate 1). No
    coverlet or other coverage/runner extras are added.

    Project reference: exactly ONE, to the API host project
    (src/DnnMigration.Api). Because Api references DnnMigration.Application and
    DnnMigration.Infrastructure (which in turn reference DnnMigration.Domain), all
    four src projects - and thus DnnDbContext, IJwtService, IPasswordHasher, the
    entities, the DTOs and ApiResponse<T> - are available transitively. The other
    three src projects are therefore NOT referenced explicitly (doing so would be
    redundant). The build-order dependency (src before tests) is resolved at the
    backend/DnnMigration.sln level, not here.

    Structure reference only (NOT a 1:1 port): the legacy VB.NET project
    Library/DotNetNuke.Library.vbproj merely confirms this is a project file. No
    legacy MSBuild-3.5 content (xmlns, ToolsVersion, ProjectGuid, Option
    Strict/Explicit, System.Web / Microsoft.VisualBasic / SqlHelper references) is
    carried over.
    ============================================================================
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing" Version="8.0.11" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.InMemory" Version="8.0.11" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.11.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" Version="2.9.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="2.8.2">
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="FluentAssertions" Version="6.12.2" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\DnnMigration.Api\DnnMigration.Api.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
